<article class="env-corollary" id="03SV">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03SV">Corollary <span data-tag="03SV">4.9.5.15</span>.</a> Let $\kappa $ be an uncountable cardinal and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category which is essentially $\kappa $-small. Then the core $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\simeq }$ is an essentially $\kappa $-small Kan complex. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\simeq }$ is a replete subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (Proposition <a data-tag="01D4" href="/tag/01D4">4.4.3.6</a>), this is a special case of Proposition <a data-tag="03SU" href="/tag/03SU">4.9.5.14</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
